thread:
Renee Ortiz: Noticed a clutch UX issue on tiny viewports: when the sidebar auto-collapses and the action bar switches to compact mode, table rows occasionally get a horizontal scroll and keyboard focus moves off the selected row. Screenshot: https://staging.redwood.internal/ux/frag-517.png

Marco Li: Repro on iPhone SE and narrow Chrome emulation. The problem seems tied to how the action bar reduces width and pushes the table; it's changing the scrollWidth mid-frame.

Anya Becker: For touch, Chrome shows a second scrollbar which is confusing. Accessibility: keyboard users lose visible focus because focus outline lands outside the scrolled container. We should ensure focus is scrolled into view after layout change.

Theo Morgan: Quick plan: prevent the top-bar from contributing to intrinsic layout when collapsed. We can make it position: absolute/sticky and keep the main grid's width stable. Also add a JS fallback: after toggle, call element.scrollIntoView({block: 'nearest'}) on the focused cell.

Renee Ortiz: Prefer CSS-first solution to avoid jank. If we do scrollIntoView, wrap it in requestAnimationFrame and only when focus moves. Also consider adding a small delay before re-enabling transitions to avoid layout thrash.

Marco Li: CSS snippet I'm testing in staging: 
```css
.header-toolbar { position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 5; }
.main-content { contain: layout; }
@media (max-width: 360px) {
  .toolbar-button-label { display: none; }
  .toolbar-button { min-width: 44px; }
}
```
This preserves main-content width and keeps tap targets.

Anya Becker: A11y checklist: aria-label on icon buttons, visible focus indicator, ensure overflow menu has role="menu" and keyboard support. Also don't hide labels for screen readers; use visually-hidden text for aria-labels.

A11y-Bot: Reminder: avoid removing transitions if users have prefers-reduced-motion. Tagging this thread for accessibility review.

Theo Morgan: UX decision: keep Copy action visible (analytics show it's highest frequency) and move Export + Details to overflow. That should reduce toolbar width. Thoughts?

Renee Ortiz: Agree. Make Copy an icon with inline tooltip on long-press. Tooltip text: 'Copy ID'. For keyboard, support Enter/Space to copy and announce via aria-live region 'Copied ID'.

Marco Li: I'll push the CSS change + small JS scrollIntoView fallback to feature/compact-toolbar. Will include visual diffs for 320px and 360px.

Anya Becker: I'll run quick a11y smoke: VoiceOver, TalkBack, keyboard nav. Putting it on my queue for tomorrow morning.

Renee Ortiz: Thanks team. Let's get this into canary once tests pass. If we still see scrollbars, we may need to clamp column widths with ellipsis for the most volatile columns.
